cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Loomground: a declarative language for the governance of AI systems and AI agents"
message: "If you use Loomground, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Loomground Contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/flxk1/loomground-governance"
abstract: >
  Loomground is a declarative language for expressing governance constraints
  on AI systems and AI agents. A governance program is a patch of
  typed nodes wired by typed cords, evaluated from its source gates, resolved at
  one master before any action takes effect, and recorded such that later
  alteration is detectable. The evaluation of the patch is the control.
keywords:
  - AI governance
  - declarative language
  - human oversight
  - provenance
  - capability security
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: "https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0"
version: 0.8.2
date-released: 2026-07-24
